{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"dd1c23f7a1027bb1","type":"group","x":492,"y":-762,"width":1647,"height":887,"label":"Experience "},
		{"id":"53cae4cef95bca2f","type":"text","text":"### These experiences can have associated confidence, fear, etc\nThis will effect model's performance ","x":907,"y":-683,"width":422,"height":136},
		{"id":"763fa9377ec36307","type":"text","text":"# How to build experiences? ","x":697,"y":-348,"width":260,"height":93,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"baabcda9c6f39322","type":"text","text":"### Experience\n(Experience of solving / victory of solving / defeat, etc)","x":576,"y":-127,"width":276,"height":151},
		{"id":"00e9297a6f33b166","type":"text","text":"Can have a ==model/agent for managing experiences==\nLike removing insignificant experiences(not yielding results)\nGiving preference to some experiences","x":1035,"y":-523,"width":304,"height":200},
		{"id":"380530996f70bbbc","type":"text","text":"#### In humans ==memory and experience are slightly different== \nBut what is experience?\nWhat is memory?\n###### Current idea is \"experiences use memories to process\"","x":563,"y":-714,"width":320,"height":277},
		{"id":"8bded3058e3cfe57","type":"text","text":"### The model itself could be a part of a game engine\n- This is much better/efficient in terms of rendering visual data from the model and for the model\n- Other forms can also be rendered ","x":1756,"y":-671,"width":342,"height":259},
		{"id":"e69295181bd7ea7f","type":"text","text":"### ==Forgetting==(not taking into account) of experiences and memories while inference \nBoth short term and long term ","x":1036,"y":-306,"width":300,"height":228},
		{"id":"14c7226c651e533c","type":"text","text":"### ==Model should use a few experiences and (or) memories for solution== \nSimilar to ==Short term memory==\n- It should query experiences from ==long term memories== and (or) Experiences\n- Accordingly there should be a ==forgetting==","x":1360,"y":-675,"width":345,"height":321,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"35a786e23933123d","type":"text","text":"##### How to point to other  experiences,\n#### experiences should process data,\n##### How to send processed data to the other experiences \n##### How should experiences use memories \n##### How should experiences create memories using the processed data","x":1352,"y":-338,"width":417,"height":306,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"fe6f4230e8852772","type":"text","text":"# Model's view of ==Problem / Input==\nCan be the of something that can be extracted from input (it can also be done with experiences too)","x":51,"y":173,"width":329,"height":207},
		{"id":"c89666bbc29e126e","type":"text","text":"## Model to use experience to solve \n### or point to another experience ","x":505,"y":221,"width":414,"height":168},
		{"id":"bea50721bcad5105","type":"text","text":"# Solution \nwith confidence ","x":1141,"y":253,"width":193,"height":107},
		{"id":"9bdb8e83fdd8285c","type":"text","text":"### More depth/parameters of a model more processing/thinking done","x":1008,"y":661,"width":456,"height":103},
		{"id":"f85b2a8488f272ce","type":"text","text":"##### Can be connected to other processing nodes to process/ think more\n\n###### - but tranfering data **must** be interpretable between nodes","x":989,"y":872,"width":363,"height":201}
	],
